IO-22: reject an RDII unit hydrograph with a negative recession limb ratio K

The [HYDROGRAPHS] validation copied legacy validateRdii(), which only
rejected a negative time to peak, so K < 0 ran with a hydrograph cut off on
its rising limb (volume (1+K)*R) and K <= -1 with no RDII at all. A base time
shorter than the time to peak is now ERROR 151 (invalid time base), and a
zero base time only means "no UH" when the time to peak is zero too. Same
rule as the 5.3.0 patch.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-22_swmm600.patch

